{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.90c5132230","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-649","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Rahman is a Nigerian composer.</li><li>In 1993, Rahman wrote <i>Paper House</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Paper House</i> uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.</li><li><i>Paper House</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.</li><li>Rahman trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of Paper House.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Paper House</i>, a symphony by Rahman, uses only percussion instruments in its second movement.","<i>Paper House</i> was written in 1993.","<i>Paper House</i> received a standing ovation at its premiere.","Viktor Rahman trained as a concert pianist."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.3dccde480a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-4","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Kowalski is a marine biologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Kowalski recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Kowalski found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Kowalski concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","Marine biologist Nadia Kowalski set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.","To investigate the question, Kowalski recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.93f06b6e94","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-24","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Nakamura is a materials scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Nakamura coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Nakamura found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Nakamura concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Materials scientist Ingrid Nakamura set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","To investigate the question, Nakamura coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.89739fdf01","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-25","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Takeda is a materials scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Materials scientist Elias Takeda set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9412af62dd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-28","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Okafor is a materials scientist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Okafor coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Okafor found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Okafor concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Materials scientist Ayumi Okafor set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.","Okafor concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Okafor coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Okafor found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.0e5d1be6ea","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-35","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Entomologist Dmitri Solberg set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6f81977ba3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-40","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Delacroix is a sociologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sociologist Imani Delacroix set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.","Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9aa4f9acb6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-51","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Abara is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Abara asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Abara found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Abara concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","To investigate the question, Abara asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Abara found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Nutrition researcher Priya Abara set out to learn whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a9bc8e4bf6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-96","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Brennan is an education researcher.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","To investigate the question, Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Hana Brennan set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.856e3c4cc3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-121","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is an ornithologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Ornithologist Tomás Ferreira set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.757cd8dedb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-134","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Duarte is an archaeologist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Duarte analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Duarte found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Duarte concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Duarte found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","To investigate the question, Duarte analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Archaeologist Ravi Duarte set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.2457e34a37","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-136","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Mbeki is an archaeologist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Mbeki analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Mbeki found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mbeki concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Archaeologist Diego Mbeki set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.","Mbeki found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","To investigate the question, Mbeki analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.43da8cfe69","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-173","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Maren Iyer is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Forest ecologist Maren Iyer set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.7c8d7377ed","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-175","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Nakamura is a music researcher.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","Music researcher Omar Nakamura set out to learn whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.","Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
